Z||000016||ChadMan||06-05-2000||12:44 PM||||Hey my simian friend - before you buy a steering rack, maybe you should try replacing your front wheel bearings and races.  This made a world of difference to my 86 SE and was really inexpensive and fairly easy to do.  The original wheel bearings were pitted and the races were scored after 115K miles - plus they were loose and sloppy.||||reg||1
