Z||000019||Patrick's Dad||06-05-2000||08:40 PM||||Hi Monk,<P>Sorry for the lateness. Any decent mechanic should be able to pick up on ball joints. It's SOP here in MA for safety inspections.<P>If you have a floor jack, lift each front wheel just a few inches off the ground, grab your airborne tire by the top and bottom and shake up and down. There should be fairly little play. Rock it side to side, the same. If you get undue up and down motion, have the lowers checked. If you get undue side to side motion, get the uppers (more likely) and your steering linkage (less likely) checked.<P>I read the post about the steering damper. I don't expect it would be this, but I don't have direct experience, either. The damper is mostly for bump steer, a problem I didn't have with my '85, and my '88 only suffered bump steer when the rack went. Got the Fiero Store's unit, too. It was more precise on center than the original.||||reg||1
